    "evidence": "One CTA at (0,0) of the compiled K=N=1024 GEMM computes a 128x128 output tile with 16 K-tiles of 64. Upstream declares contiguous f16 A[M,K] and B[K,N], and allocates independent C[M,N]. Both input tensor maps have 1024-element (2048-byte) row pitches. A copies a [K,M]=[64,128] box; two B copies use [N,K]=[64,64] boxes at adjacent N coordinates. Output stores retain the full C row pitch of 1024 elements. Parameter 2 binds distinct C, not input A. PyTorch uses full contiguous A/B inputs and computes A[:128,:] @ B[:,:128], with f32 accumulation and f16 output. Input maps are identity; output mapping selects the analyzed tile.",
